From 9cf5bb23d71fe2d37f39ab697e331fe1ab1ae571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Buckles <buckles@blacksmith.sh>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 13:51:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Enable Blacksmith remote caching for Bazel builds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Move the Bazel tooling workflow to Blacksmith runners and turn on Bazel
Build Caching (a dashboard toggle — zero workflow or .bazelrc config;
Blacksmith wires up the remote cache before each job). Action and test
results are shared across branches per architecture, so warm builds skip
compilation entirely.
---
 template/.github/workflows/bazel.yml | 2 +-
 template/bazel/README.md             | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/template/.github/workflows/bazel.yml b/template/.github/workflows/bazel.yml
index dc9cce2..87e3f9a 100644
--- a/template/.github/workflows/bazel.yml
+++ b/template/.github/workflows/bazel.yml
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ on:
 jobs:
   build-and-test:
     name: Build and test
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    runs-on: blacksmith-4vcpu-ubuntu-2404
     defaults:
       run:
         working-directory: bazel
diff --git a/template/bazel/README.md b/template/bazel/README.md
index f4a0176..9842443 100644
--- a/template/bazel/README.md
+++ b/template/bazel/README.md
@@ -7,3 +7,11 @@ because it shares (planned) codegen with the data-plane team's monorepo.
 bazel build //:checksum_tool
 bazel test //:checksum_test
 ```
+
+## Remote caching
+
+CI runs on Blacksmith with **Bazel Build Caching** enabled for this repo
+(dashboard: Settings → Features → Caching). Blacksmith configures the
+remote cache automatically before each job — no `.bazelrc` changes or
+workflow config needed. Do not add an explicit `--remote_cache` flag;
+it would take precedence over the managed cache.
-- 
